INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('International Monetary Fund (IMF)', 'International Monetary Fund (IMF)', 'International Financial Institution', 'The IMF''s role in Yemen (2010-2025) has shifted from supporting economic reform and fiscal consolidation under the Extended Credit Facility (ECF) to providing emergency financial assistance and technical advice amidst a protracted conflict and humanitarian crisis. Prior to 2015, the IMF aimed to reduce the fiscal deficit and inflation. Since 2016, its engagement has been limited to concessional emergency financing (RCF) to address urgent balance of payments needs and technical assistance to the central bank to maintain core economic functions and improve governance, despite the political split.', 'The IMF''s role in Yemen (2010-2025) has shifted from supporting economic reform and fiscal consolidation under the Extended Credit Facility (ECF) to providing emergency financial assistance and technical advice amidst a protracted conflict and humanitarian crisis. Prior to 2015, the IMF aimed to reduce the fiscal deficit and inflation. Since 2016, its engagement has been limited to concessional emergency financing (RCF) to address urgent balance of payments needs and technical assistance to the central bank to maintain core economic functions and improve governance, despite the political split.', 'Website: https://www.imf.org/en/countries/yem; Resident Representative: Gazi Shbaikat (since Jan 2021, for Iraq and Yemen); General Contact: +1 (202) 623-7000 (IMF Headquarters); IMF Office in Yemen: ', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (via KSrelief and SDRPY)', 'Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (via KSrelief and SDRPY)', 'Regional Actor', 'Saudi Arabia plays a dual and dominant role in Yemen, characterized by its military leadership of the coalition intervening since 2015 and its position as the largest single donor of humanitarian and development aid. The military intervention aims to restore the internationally recognized government, while the aid, channeled primarily through the King Salman Humanitarian Aid and Relief Centre (KSrelief) and the Saudi Development and Reconstruction Program for Yemen (SDRPY), focuses on stabilizing the economy and addressing the severe humanitarian crisis. Since 2010, the Kingdom has committed billions of dollars in aid, including multi-billion dollar deposits to the Central Bank of Yemen and hundreds of projects across vital sectors like health, education, and food security, making it a central, yet controversial, actor in the country''s trajectory.', 'Saudi Arabia plays a dual and dominant role in Yemen, characterized by its military leadership of the coalition intervening since 2015 and its position as the largest single donor of humanitarian and development aid. The military intervention aims to restore the internationally recognized government, while the aid, channeled primarily through the King Salman Humanitarian Aid and Relief Centre (KSrelief) and the Saudi Development and Reconstruction Program for Yemen (SDRPY), focuses on stabilizing the economy and addressing the severe humanitarian crisis. Since 2010, the Kingdom has committed billions of dollars in aid, including multi-billion dollar deposits to the Central Bank of Yemen and hundreds of projects across vital sectors like health, education, and food security, making it a central, yet controversial, actor in the country''s trajectory.', 'KSrelief Website: https://www.ksrelief.org/en, KSrelief Email: info@ksrelief.org, KSrelief Phone: + 966 920 008 554, KSrelief Address: King Abdullah Road, Riyadh 123717046 [18]; SDRPY Website: https:/', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('United Arab Emirates (UAE)', 'United Arab Emirates (UAE)', 'Regional Actor', 'The United Arab Emirates (UAE) has been a central, yet complex, regional actor in Yemen since 2015, initially as a key military partner in the Saudi-led coalition to restore the internationally recognized government. Its role has evolved from direct military intervention to a strategic focus on counter-terrorism, particularly against Al-Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula (AQAP), and securing vital maritime interests along the Red Sea and Gulf of Aden. Economically, the UAE has provided over $6 billion in aid, including a significant $2 billion pledge to the Central Bank of Yemen, aimed at stabilizing the collapsing economy and supporting humanitarian needs. However, its political support for local proxy forces, such as the Southern Transitional Council (STC), has introduced a separatist dimension to the conflict, complicating the political landscape and the path to a unified resolution.', 'The United Arab Emirates (UAE) has been a central, yet complex, regional actor in Yemen since 2015, initially as a key military partner in the Saudi-led coalition to restore the internationally recognized government. Its role has evolved from direct military intervention to a strategic focus on counter-terrorism, particularly against Al-Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula (AQAP), and securing vital maritime interests along the Red Sea and Gulf of Aden. Economically, the UAE has provided over $6 billion in aid, including a significant $2 billion pledge to the Central Bank of Yemen, aimed at stabilizing the collapsing economy and supporting humanitarian needs. However, its political support for local proxy forces, such as the Southern Transitional Council (STC), has introduced a separatist dimension to the conflict, complicating the political landscape and the path to a unified resolution.', 'UAE Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFA) Aid Portal: uaeaidportal@mofa.gov.ae; UAE Embassy in Sana''a (Currently closed/limited operations): Circle Line Aljinobi (behind Central Security), Sana''a, Yeme', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) Yemen', 'UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) Yemen', 'UN Agency', 'The UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) in Yemen serves as the central coordinating body for the humanitarian response from 2010 to 2025, leading the development and implementation of the annual Humanitarian Needs and Response Plan (HNRP). OCHA''s mandate is to mobilize and coordinate effective and principled humanitarian action in partnership with national and international actors, ensuring aid reaches the most vulnerable populations affected by conflict, economic collapse, and natural disasters. A key function is managing the Yemen Humanitarian Fund (YHF), which has channeled billions of dollars in aid to life-saving and life-sustaining activities across the country, making OCHA instrumental in mitigating the world''s largest humanitarian crisis.', 'The UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) in Yemen serves as the central coordinating body for the humanitarian response from 2010 to 2025, leading the development and implementation of the annual Humanitarian Needs and Response Plan (HNRP). OCHA''s mandate is to mobilize and coordinate effective and principled humanitarian action in partnership with national and international actors, ensuring aid reaches the most vulnerable populations affected by conflict, economic collapse, and natural disasters. A key function is managing the Yemen Humanitarian Fund (YHF), which has channeled billions of dollars in aid to life-saving and life-sustaining activities across the country, making OCHA instrumental in mitigating the world''s largest humanitarian crisis.', 'Website: https://www.unocha.org/yemen; Office Email: ochayemen@un.org; YHF Email: yemenhpf@un.org; UN in Yemen Address: Beside Sixty Road, near Alawqaf complex, P.O. Box: 551, Sana''a, Yemen; UN in Ye', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) Yemen', 'United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) Yemen', 'UN Agency', 'UNDP Yemen serves as a critical UN Agency bridging the humanitarian-development-peace nexus, focusing on long-term resilience and recovery alongside urgent humanitarian needs. Its mandate centers on restoring livelihoods, strengthening institutional and economic resilience, and laying the foundation for sustainable development while addressing profound gender inequalities. Key activities include implementing large-scale joint programs like ERRY and SIERY to support local governance, basic service delivery, and economic recovery through job creation and SME support. The impact is quantified by reaching millions of Yemenis with improved access to services and creating thousands of employment opportunities, positioning UNDP as a central actor in Yemen''s post-conflict and economic stabilization efforts.', 'UNDP Yemen serves as a critical UN Agency bridging the humanitarian-development-peace nexus, focusing on long-term resilience and recovery alongside urgent humanitarian needs. Its mandate centers on restoring livelihoods, strengthening institutional and economic resilience, and laying the foundation for sustainable development while addressing profound gender inequalities. Key activities include implementing large-scale joint programs like ERRY and SIERY to support local governance, basic service delivery, and economic recovery through job creation and SME support. The impact is quantified by reaching millions of Yemenis with improved access to services and creating thousands of employment opportunities, positioning UNDP as a central actor in Yemen''s post-conflict and economic stabilization efforts.', 'Website: https://www.undp.org/yemen; Address: Beside Sixty Road, near Alawqaf complex P.O. Box 551, Sana''a, Yemen; E-mail: rbas-info@undp.org [8] [9]', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('World Food Programme (WFP)', 'World Food Programme (WFP)', 'UN Agency', 'The World Food Programme (WFP) has been a central actor in Yemen''s humanitarian crisis since 2010, with its role dramatically escalating after the 2015 conflict, making it WFP''s second-largest global operation. Its primary mandate is to provide emergency food assistance, nutrition support, and resilience-building activities to millions of food-insecure Yemenis. WFP''s activities have been crucial in preventing widespread famine, but the operation has been consistently hampered by critical funding shortages and complex operational challenges, including access issues and disagreements with local authorities. The agency''s work has shifted from broad emergency response to more targeted, life-saving, and resilience-focused interventions in response to resource constraints and the protracted nature of the crisis.', 'The World Food Programme (WFP) has been a central actor in Yemen''s humanitarian crisis since 2010, with its role dramatically escalating after the 2015 conflict, making it WFP''s second-largest global operation. Its primary mandate is to provide emergency food assistance, nutrition support, and resilience-building activities to millions of food-insecure Yemenis. WFP''s activities have been crucial in preventing widespread famine, but the operation has been consistently hampered by critical funding shortages and complex operational challenges, including access issues and disagreements with local authorities. The agency''s work has shifted from broad emergency response to more targeted, life-saving, and resilience-focused interventions in response to resource constraints and the protracted nature of the crisis.', 'Website: https://www.wfp.org/countries/yemen; Email: wfp.yemen@wfp.org (via UN Yemen contact page) [10] [11]', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('UNICEF Yemen', 'UNICEF Yemen', 'UN Agency', 'UNICEF Yemen operates as a leading humanitarian and development actor, focusing on the rights and well-being of children and women across the country. Since the escalation of conflict in 2015, its mandate has primarily shifted to providing life-saving, protective, and multisectoral interventions, co-leading key humanitarian clusters like WASH, Nutrition, and Child Protection. The agency works to strengthen essential public services, such as health and education, which have been severely weakened by the protracted crisis, while also implementing social protection and emergency cash transfer programs. UNICEF''s role is critical in mitigating the impact of conflict, economic collapse, and climate-related shocks on Yemen''s most vulnerable population.', 'UNICEF Yemen operates as a leading humanitarian and development actor, focusing on the rights and well-being of children and women across the country. Since the escalation of conflict in 2015, its mandate has primarily shifted to providing life-saving, protective, and multisectoral interventions, co-leading key humanitarian clusters like WASH, Nutrition, and Child Protection. The agency works to strengthen essential public services, such as health and education, which have been severely weakened by the protracted crisis, while also implementing social protection and emergency cash transfer programs. UNICEF''s role is critical in mitigating the impact of conflict, economic collapse, and climate-related shocks on Yemen''s most vulnerable population.', 'Website: https://www.unicef.org/yemen/', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('World Health Organization (WHO) Yemen', 'World Health Organization (WHO) Yemen', 'UN Agency', 'The World Health Organization (WHO) Yemen leads the UN Health Cluster response, focusing on preventing the collapse of the country''s health system amidst the ongoing conflict (2014-2025). Its primary activities include sustaining essential health services, responding to major disease outbreaks like cholera and COVID-19, and supporting the health workforce through training and financial aid. WHO''s role is critical in providing life-saving medical care, strengthening disease surveillance, and addressing acute malnutrition and other health crises for millions of vulnerable Yemenis.', 'The World Health Organization (WHO) Yemen leads the UN Health Cluster response, focusing on preventing the collapse of the country''s health system amidst the ongoing conflict (2014-2025). Its primary activities include sustaining essential health services, responding to major disease outbreaks like cholera and COVID-19, and supporting the health workforce through training and financial aid. WHO''s role is critical in providing life-saving medical care, strengthening disease surveillance, and addressing acute malnutrition and other health crises for millions of vulnerable Yemenis.', 'Website: https://www.who.int/countries/yem; Address: PO Box 543, Sana''a [3]', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('U.S. Agency for International Development (USAID)', 'U.S. Agency for International Development (USAID)', 'International Development Agency / Bilateral Donor', 'USAID is the largest bilateral donor of humanitarian and development assistance to Yemen, with a mandate to address the underlying causes of instability and support the country''s transition. Since the escalation of the conflict in 2015, its primary focus has shifted to providing critical, life-saving humanitarian aid, while also maintaining targeted development programs in health, WASH, education, and economic growth. The agency works with international and local partners to rebuild social and economic institutions, aiming to foster future resilience and lay a foundation for durable peace and prosperity.', 'USAID is the largest bilateral donor of humanitarian and development assistance to Yemen, with a mandate to address the underlying causes of instability and support the country''s transition. Since the escalation of the conflict in 2015, its primary focus has shifted to providing critical, life-saving humanitarian aid, while also maintaining targeted development programs in health, WASH, education, and economic growth. The agency works with international and local partners to rebuild social and economic institutions, aiming to foster future resilience and lay a foundation for durable peace and prosperity.', 'Website: https://www.usaid.gov/yemen; Country Director: Kimberlee Bell (as of 2024); General USAID Contact: 1-202-712-4300', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) - United Kingdom', 'Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) - United Kingdom', 'Governmental Development Agency', 'The FCDO (formerly DFID) is a key player in Yemen, focusing on diplomatic efforts to broker peace and providing life-saving humanitarian assistance. Its strategy is guided by four aims: advancing peace, alleviating the humanitarian crisis, boosting economic stability, and promoting security. The UK holds the pen on Yemen-related issues at the UN Security Council, leveraging its diplomatic influence alongside its role as one of the largest humanitarian donors. The FCDO''s activities shifted from long-term development to large-scale humanitarian response following the 2015 conflict, though it has recently re-emphasized economic stability and recovery.', 'The FCDO (formerly DFID) is a key player in Yemen, focusing on diplomatic efforts to broker peace and providing life-saving humanitarian assistance. Its strategy is guided by four aims: advancing peace, alleviating the humanitarian crisis, boosting economic stability, and promoting security. The UK holds the pen on Yemen-related issues at the UN Security Council, leveraging its diplomatic influence alongside its role as one of the largest humanitarian donors. The FCDO''s activities shifted from long-term development to large-scale humanitarian response following the 2015 conflict, though it has recently re-emphasized economic stability and recovery.', 'Website: https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office; DevTracker: https://devtracker.fcdo.gov.uk/countries/YE', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('European Union (EU)', 'European Union (EU)', 'Regional Actor / International Donor', 'The European Union is a longstanding partner and one of the leading international donors to Yemen, with its engagement structured around three core pillars: political, humanitarian, and development support. Since the escalation of the conflict in 2015, the EU has provided approximately €1.6 billion in aid, focusing on life-saving humanitarian assistance and long-term resilience-building. Politically, the EU actively supports the UN-led peace process, advocating for an inclusive political settlement and the promotion of human rights. Its development cooperation, exemplified by the ERRY Joint Programme, aims to strengthen livelihoods, restore basic services, and promote economic stability and peacebuilding in vulnerable communities.', 'The European Union is a longstanding partner and one of the leading international donors to Yemen, with its engagement structured around three core pillars: political, humanitarian, and development support. Since the escalation of the conflict in 2015, the EU has provided approximately €1.6 billion in aid, focusing on life-saving humanitarian assistance and long-term resilience-building. Politically, the EU actively supports the UN-led peace process, advocating for an inclusive political settlement and the promotion of human rights. Its development cooperation, exemplified by the ERRY Joint Programme, aims to strengthen livelihoods, restore basic services, and promote economic stability and peacebuilding in vulnerable communities.', 'Website: https://www.eeas.europa.eu/yemen/', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Islamic Republic of Iran', 'Islamic Republic of Iran', 'Regional Actor / Non-State Actor Sponsor', 'Iran''s role in Yemen is primarily that of a state sponsor to the Ansar Allah (Houthi) movement, focusing on political, military, and financial support rather than formal economic or humanitarian aid. The Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps-Qods Force (IRGC-QF) is the main implementing body, providing training, advanced weaponry, and advisory support, which has been instrumental in transforming the Houthis into a powerful regional actor. This support, estimated at hundreds of millions of dollars annually through illicit networks, has sustained the Houthi war effort and their control over northern Yemen, significantly contributing to the protracted conflict and regional instability. Iran''s involvement is a strategic move to counter regional rivals and project power into the Arabian Peninsula and the Red Sea.', 'Iran''s role in Yemen is primarily that of a state sponsor to the Ansar Allah (Houthi) movement, focusing on political, military, and financial support rather than formal economic or humanitarian aid. The Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps-Qods Force (IRGC-QF) is the main implementing body, providing training, advanced weaponry, and advisory support, which has been instrumental in transforming the Houthis into a powerful regional actor. This support, estimated at hundreds of millions of dollars annually through illicit networks, has sustained the Houthi war effort and their control over northern Yemen, significantly contributing to the protracted conflict and regional instability. Iran''s involvement is a strategic move to counter regional rivals and project power into the Arabian Peninsula and the Red Sea.', 'Website: https://en.mfa.ir/ (Ministry of Foreign Affairs); https://newyork.mfa.ir/ (Permanent Mission to the UN)', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Sultanate of Oman', 'Sultanate of Oman', 'Regional Actor/Mediator', 'The Sultanate of Oman has played a vital and unique role in the Yemen crisis (2010-2025) by maintaining strict neutrality and refusing to join the Saudi-led coalition, which has positioned it as the most trusted and effective regional mediator. Its primary activity is diplomatic, facilitating back-channel negotiations between the Houthi movement, Saudi Arabia, and the internationally recognized government, leading to significant de-escalation efforts and prisoner exchanges. Beyond mediation, Oman provides consistent humanitarian and relief assistance, primarily through the Oman Charitable Organization (OCO), focusing on the border governorates of Al Mahra and Hadhramaut. This dual role of diplomatic facilitator and humanitarian supporter underscores Oman''s commitment to regional stability and the welfare of the Yemeni people.', 'The Sultanate of Oman has played a vital and unique role in the Yemen crisis (2010-2025) by maintaining strict neutrality and refusing to join the Saudi-led coalition, which has positioned it as the most trusted and effective regional mediator. Its primary activity is diplomatic, facilitating back-channel negotiations between the Houthi movement, Saudi Arabia, and the internationally recognized government, leading to significant de-escalation efforts and prisoner exchanges. Beyond mediation, Oman provides consistent humanitarian and relief assistance, primarily through the Oman Charitable Organization (OCO), focusing on the border governorates of Al Mahra and Hadhramaut. This dual role of diplomatic facilitator and humanitarian supporter underscores Oman''s commitment to regional stability and the welfare of the Yemeni people.', 'Ministry of Foreign Affairs Website: https://www.fm.gov.om/; Oman Charitable Organization (OCO) Website: https://www.oco.org.om/; OCO Phone: +968 24297994; OCO Head Office: Al Khuwair, adjacent to Sul', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Southern Transitional Council (STC)', 'Southern Transitional Council (STC)', 'Non-State Actor (Secessionist Political and Military Organization)', 'The Southern Transitional Council (STC) is a UAE-backed secessionist political and military organization established in 2017 with the core mandate of achieving self-determination and restoring the independent state of South Yemen [1] [4]. The STC''s role in Yemen''s economy is characterized by its control over key economic infrastructure, particularly the Aden port and surrounding checkpoints, from which it generates significant revenue through taxes and levies [5]. While it has contributed to counter-terrorism efforts and achieved political integration as a key member of the Presidential Leadership Council (PLC), its actions have also been cited for exacerbating the economic crisis and failing to significantly improve public service delivery in the areas under its control [16] [17]. The STC remains a central, and often destabilizing, actor in the conflict, with its military and political maneuvers directly impacting the humanitarian and economic landscape of southern Yemen [11].', 'The Southern Transitional Council (STC) is a UAE-backed secessionist political and military organization established in 2017 with the core mandate of achieving self-determination and restoring the independent state of South Yemen [1] [4]. The STC''s role in Yemen''s economy is characterized by its control over key economic infrastructure, particularly the Aden port and surrounding checkpoints, from which it generates significant revenue through taxes and levies [5]. While it has contributed to counter-terrorism efforts and achieved political integration as a key member of the Presidential Leadership Council (PLC), its actions have also been cited for exacerbating the economic crisis and failing to significantly improve public service delivery in the areas under its control [16] [17]. The STC remains a central, and often destabilizing, actor in the conflict, with its military and political maneuvers directly impacting the humanitarian and economic landscape of southern Yemen [11].', 'Website: https://en.stcaden.com/; STC-USA Office: https://stcus.org/; Email (STC-USA): info@stcus.org', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Central Bank of Yemen (Aden)', 'Central Bank of Yemen (Aden)', 'Central Bank / Financial Institution (De Facto)', 'The Central Bank of Yemen (CBY) in Aden, established following the 2016 split, functions as the central bank for the internationally recognized government, aiming to maintain currency stability and regulate banking activities in government-controlled areas. Its primary role has been to manage the severe economic fallout of the conflict, including hyperinflation and currency depreciation, by implementing monetary policy and seeking external financial support. The CBY Aden''s activities are critical for the economy, particularly in facilitating the import of essential goods and attempting to unify the fragmented financial system.', 'The Central Bank of Yemen (CBY) in Aden, established following the 2016 split, functions as the central bank for the internationally recognized government, aiming to maintain currency stability and regulate banking activities in government-controlled areas. Its primary role has been to manage the severe economic fallout of the conflict, including hyperinflation and currency depreciation, by implementing monetary policy and seeking external financial support. The CBY Aden''s activities are critical for the economy, particularly in facilitating the import of essential goods and attempting to unify the fragmented financial system.', 'Website: https://www.english.cby-ye.com/; Headquarters: Head Office - Aden, Republic of Yemen', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('Central Bank of Yemen (Sanaa)', 'Central Bank of Yemen (Sanaa)', 'De Facto Monetary Authority / Central Bank Branch', 'The Central Bank of Yemen (Sanaa) operates as the de facto monetary authority in Houthi-controlled areas following the 2016 split. It maintains the original CBY''s physical assets and human resources, overseeing the country''s largest financial and population centers. Its primary function is to manage monetary policy, secure revenue streams for the de facto authorities, and regulate the banking sector through coercive measures. Key activities include enforcing a separate monetary zone with a stable exchange rate for the ''old'' rial, banning the use of new rials, and pursuing the "Islamization" of the financial system.', 'The Central Bank of Yemen (Sanaa) operates as the de facto monetary authority in Houthi-controlled areas following the 2016 split. It maintains the original CBY''s physical assets and human resources, overseeing the country''s largest financial and population centers. Its primary function is to manage monetary policy, secure revenue streams for the de facto authorities, and regulate the banking sector through coercive measures. Key activities include enforcing a separate monetary zone with a stable exchange rate for the ''old'' rial, banning the use of new rials, and pursuing the "Islamization" of the financial system.', 'PO Box 59, Sana''a, Republic of Yemen (Original CBY address, current status unconfirmed); Phone: +967 (1) 274310 to 274318 (Original CBY number, current status unconfirmed)', true);

INSERT INTO actors (nameEn, nameAr, type, descriptionEn, descriptionAr, website, active)
VALUES ('State of Qatar (via Qatar Fund for Development, Qatar Charity, and Qatar Red Crescent Society)', 'State of Qatar (via Qatar Fund for Development, Qatar Charity, and Qatar Red Crescent Society)', 'Regional Actor', 'The State of Qatar, primarily through the Qatar Fund for Development (QFFD), Qatar Charity (QC), and Qatar Red Crescent Society (QRCS), has played a dual role in Yemen, encompassing both diplomatic mediation and significant humanitarian and development aid. From 2010 to 2025, Qatar''s government and non-governmental organizations have provided over $600 million in aid, focusing on relief, food security, water, sanitation, and health. Qatar also engaged in early peace mediation, notably brokering a deal in 2010, and later restored diplomatic ties in 2021 after a period of strained relations. The aid efforts are characterized by large-scale funding pledges to UN agencies and direct implementation of projects by Qatari NGOs, aiming to alleviate the severe humanitarian crisis and foster economic empowerment.', 'The State of Qatar, primarily through the Qatar Fund for Development (QFFD), Qatar Charity (QC), and Qatar Red Crescent Society (QRCS), has played a dual role in Yemen, encompassing both diplomatic mediation and significant humanitarian and development aid. From 2010 to 2025, Qatar''s government and non-governmental organizations have provided over $600 million in aid, focusing on relief, food security, water, sanitation, and health. Qatar also engaged in early peace mediation, notably brokering a deal in 2010, and later restored diplomatic ties in 2021 after a period of strained relations. The aid efforts are characterized by large-scale funding pledges to UN agencies and direct implementation of projects by Qatari NGOs, aiming to alleviate the severe humanitarian crisis and foster economic empowerment.', 'Qatar Fund for Development (QFFD): Website: https://www.qatarfund.org.qa/
Qatar Charity (QC): Website: https://www.qcharity.org/
Qatar Red Crescent Society (QRCS): Website: https://www.qrcs.org.qa/', true);

